  "description": "MySQL for .NET apps on Entity Framework Core: `UseRaskMySql(...)` wraps Oracle's `UseMySQL` provider, applies a lock-wait and a SELECT execution timeout on every connection the context opens, sets a client command timeout, and turns on transient-failure retrying. SQLite stays Rask's default; this is for when MySQL is the house database.",
